{"reference":"Ecclesiastes 11","book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":11,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Joy and accountability","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The call to rejoice in life, including youth, is not presented as careless pleasure. Ecclesiastes treats joy as a human portion and a gift enabled by God amid circumstances people cannot control, while also holding together God’s judgment and human accountability. That combination helps explain why verses 7–10 can warmly commend enjoyment of life yet immediately add a sober reminder that one’s choices matter.","verse_refs":["Ecclesiastes 11:7-10","Ecclesiastes 11:9"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ecclesiastes_011_f9147b5bda254240d8e6063b"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}